    <string name="health_atlas_distribution_rates">k12 = %1$s h⁻¹; k21 = %2$s h⁻¹; k10 = %3$s h⁻¹.</string>
    <string name="health_atlas_distribution_formula">dA1/dt = −(k10 + k12)A1 + k21A2\ndA2/dt = k12A1 − k21A2\nA1(0) = 100; A2(0) = 0\nEliminated = 100 − A1 − A2</string>
    <string name="health_atlas_distribution_boundary">Fixed first-order rate constants; no absorption, repeat dosing, saturation or patient fitting. Slider ranges are teaching inputs, not clinical ranges. No dose, treatment effect or personal organ exposure is calculated.</string>
